{number: 32}
{title: Jesus, Keep Me Near the Cross}
{key: F}

{start_of_verse: 1}
[F] Jesus, keep me near the cross;
[Bb] There a precious [F] fountain,
Free to all, a healing stream,
Flows from [C7] Calvary's [F] mountain.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
In the [F] cross, in the [Bb] cross,
[F] Be my glory [C7] ever,
Till my [F] raptured soul shall [Bb] find
[F] Rest be-[C7] yond the [F] river.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: 2}
[F] Near the cross, a trembling soul,
[Bb] Love and mercy [F] found me;
There the bright and morning star
Sheds its [C7] beams a-[F] round me.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
[F] Near the cross! O Lamb of God,
[Bb] Bring its scenes be-[F] fore me;
Help me walk from day to day
With its [C7] shadow [F] o'er me.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 4}
[F] Near the cross I'll watch and wait,
[Bb] Hoping, trusting [F] ever,
Till I reach the golden strand
Just be-[C7] yond the [F] river.
{end_of_verse}
